From: well0nez <well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] h713: size the scanout carveout for the panel, not for 720p

uboot-scanout is 8 MiB because two 1280x720 ARGB8888 frames are 7.03 MiB.
That is board B's panel. This board's is 1920x1080, where one frame is
7.91 MiB: the front slot fits with 92 KiB to spare and there is no room at
all for a back slot, so the only thing that can be built on this carveout is
single-buffered scanout, which tears.

Measured on hardware, gles-play at 1920x1080 through the VE and the GPU:

    carveout 0x6c100000 + 8192 KiB, slot 8100 KiB
    carveout holds 8192 KiB, two 8100 KiB slots need 16200 KiB
    2411 frames in 40581 ms (59.41 fps), 0 commit timeouts

so decode and present already run at the panel's vsync ceiling; what is
missing is somewhere to put the second buffer. 16 MiB covers two 1080p slots
with 184 KiB left over, and costs 8 MiB of a gibibyte.

The exporter's default size moves with it. It is a module parameter and could
be overridden at load time, but a default that disagrees with the reservation
it describes is a trap: that bound is the only thing between a userspace
ioctl and memory the page allocator has handed to something else.

A 720p board keeps working; it reserves 8 MiB it does not need. Sizing the
reservation from the panel would be better, but the panel size is not known
until the MIPS co-processor has run, which is long after the devicetree is
parsed.

Signed-off-by: well0nez <well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi	2026-09-01 00:01:19.339927690 +0200
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi	2026-09-01 00:01:31.042980668 +0200
@@ -110,9 +110,17 @@
 		 * CMA instead, because a dma-coherent pool allocates in
 		 * power-of-two page orders -- a 3.6 MiB framebuffer takes a
 		 * 4 MiB slot, so 16 MiB yielded exactly four and mpv ran out.
+		 *
+		 * 16 MiB, not 8: a slot is one full ARGB8888 frame at the
+		 * panel's size, and this panel is 1920x1080, so a slot is
+		 * 7.91 MiB and two of them need 15.82 MiB. At 8 MiB only the
+		 * front slot fits, which forces single-buffered scanout and
+		 * tears. Keep this in step with sunxi_scanout_dmabuf's
+		 * scanout_size default -- that is the bound its ioctl checks
+		 * a userspace request against.
 		 */
 		framebuf_reserved: uboot-scanout@6c100000 {
-			reg = <0x6c100000 0x800000>;
+			reg = <0x6c100000 0x1000000>;
 			no-map;
 		};
 	};
--- a/drivers/misc/sunxi-scanout-dmabuf.c	2026-09-01 00:01:19.340643872 +0200
+++ b/drivers/misc/sunxi-scanout-dmabuf.c	2026-09-01 00:01:31.043103428 +0200
@@ -47,7 +47,11 @@
 };
 
 static u64 scanout_phys = 0x6c100000ULL;
-static u64 scanout_size = 0x800000ULL;          /* both buffers */
+/*
+ * Both buffers. A slot is one full ARGB8888 frame at panel size: 3.52 MiB
+ * at 1280x720, 7.91 MiB at 1920x1080. Must match uboot-scanout in the DT.
+ */
+static u64 scanout_size = 0x1000000ULL;
 module_param(scanout_phys, ullong, 0444);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(scanout_phys, "physical base of the scanout carveout");
 module_param(scanout_size, ullong, 0444);
